      "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{csc}⁡({52}^{∘}-\\theta )$ as a cofunction of a complementary angle.",
      "worked_solution": "We know that the cofunction of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta $ is $\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ,$ and the angle complementary to ${52}^{∘}-\\theta $ is \n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}-({52}^{∘}-\\theta )={90}^{∘}-{52}^{∘}+\\theta =\\theta +{38}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\n So we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({52}^{∘}-\\theta )=\\operatorname{sec}⁡({90}^{∘}-({52}^{∘}-\\theta ))=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\theta +{38}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
